---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Obf from '../../components/Obf.astro';
import ProtectedLink from '../../components/ProtectedLink.astro';
import { contact, routes } from '../../i18n/content';
---

<Base lang="en" title="Privacy Policy – Thomas Tischner IT Systems" description="Privacy policy of Thomas Tischner IT Systems: hosted on GitHub Pages, no cookies, no tracking." alternates={{ de: routes.de.privacy }}>
  <article class="legal">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p class="note">
        This is an English translation for your convenience. Only the
        <a href={routes.de.privacy} hreflang="de">German version</a> is legally binding.
      </p>

      <p>
        In short: this website sets no cookies, uses no tracking or analytics and loads no third-party content
        (fonts are served locally). Personal data is only processed when the page is delivered and when you
        contact me by email or phone.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>The controller responsible for data processing on this website within the meaning of the GDPR is:</p>
      <address>
        <Obf text={contact.name} /><br />
        {contact.company}<br />
        <Obf text={contact.street} /><br />
        <Obf text={contact.city} /><br />
        Germany<br />
        Phone: <ProtectedLink href={contact.phoneHref} fallback="#"><Obf text={contact.phone} /></ProtectedLink><br />
        Email: <ProtectedLink href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} fallback="#"><Obf text={contact.email} /></ProtectedLink>
      </address>

      <h2>2. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided via the GitHub Pages service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
        San Francisco, CA 94107, USA (a subsidiary of Microsoft Corporation), possibly using content delivery
        networks employed by GitHub.
      </p>
      <p>When you visit the website, the following data is necessarily transmitted to and processed on GitHub’s servers:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address of the requesting device,</li>
        <li>date and time of the request,</li>
        <li>requested page or file,</li>
        <li>referrer URL (the previously visited page),</li>
        <li>browser and operating system used (user agent).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I use GitHub Pages to deliver this website reliably and securely. The legal basis is
        Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; my legitimate interest lies in the technically error-free, stable and secure
        provision of my website.
      </p>
      <p>
        According to GitHub, it stores the IP addresses of visitors to GitHub Pages sites for security purposes
        (e.g. to defend against attacks). GitHub is itself responsible for this processing. GitHub does not
        specify a retention period; according to GitHub, the data is stored for as long as necessary for
        security purposes and to comply with legal obligations. I do not receive any server log files and
        cannot identify visitors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data is transferred to the USA in the process. An adequacy decision of the European Commission exists
        for the USA (EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, Art. 45 GDPR); according to GitHub, it is certified under
        this framework. Further information can be found in
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. No cookies, no tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not use cookies or comparable technologies to store information on your device.
        There is no reach measurement, no tracking and no profiling. No external fonts, scripts or other
        third-party content are embedded.
      </p>
      <p>
        The website contains small JavaScript functions, partly embedded directly in the page and partly (the
        browser game) loaded on demand from the same server. They run exclusively locally in your browser and
        control a visual effect (a light follows the mouse pointer), the highlighting of the active navigation
        item, the assembly of the email and phone links and a small browser game that only starts at your
        request. They store no information on your device and transmit no data to me or third parties. The
        website also works without JavaScript.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Contact by email or phone</h2>
      <p>
        If you send me an email or call me, I process your details (in particular name, email address or phone
        number and the content of your request) to handle your inquiry. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR
        if your inquiry aims at concluding or performing a contract, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate
        interest in answering inquiries).
      </p>
      <p>
        I delete your data as soon as it is no longer required for processing your inquiry and no statutory
        retention obligations apply (Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR in conjunction with § 147 of the German Fiscal Code:
        up to 6 years for business correspondence, up to 8 years for accounting records).
      </p>
      <p>
        Emails are processed on the servers of my email provider WEB.DE, a service of 1&amp;1 Mail &amp; Media
        GmbH, Brauerstraße 48, 76135 Karlsruhe, Germany.
      </p>

      <h2>5. External links</h2>
      <p>
        This website contains links to external services, including my profiles on LinkedIn and GitHub, a
        certification record on Credly and my own product holzbau-konfigurator.de. Data is only transmitted to
        these services when you click a link. Their respective privacy policies then apply.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Obligation to provide data, automated decision-making</h2>
      <p>
        You are under no legal or contractual obligation to provide me with personal data. However, the website
        cannot be delivered without the technically necessary transmission of your IP address, and I cannot
        answer your inquiry without your contact details. There is no automated decision-making including
        profiling (Art. 22 GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the following rights regarding your personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>right of access (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
        <li>right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
        <li>right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
        <li>right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
        <li>right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
        <li>right to object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Right to object:</strong> Where processing is based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, you may object at any
        time on grounds relating to your particular situation. An informal message to the email address above
        is sufficient.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority
        (Art. 77 GDPR). The competent authority is the Bavarian State Office for Data Protection Supervision
        (BayLDA), Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach, Germany (postal address: Postfach 1349, 91504 Ansbach),
        <a href="https://www.lda.bayern.de/de/beschwerde.html">www.lda.bayern.de</a>.
        You may also contact the supervisory authority of your habitual residence or place of work.
      </p>

      <h2>8. SSL/TLS encryption</h2>
      <p>
        For security reasons, this website uses TLS encryption (HTTPS). You can recognize an encrypted
        connection by “https://” in your browser’s address bar.
      </p>

      <p><small>Last updated: October 2026</small></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
